"A conjectured formula for the rational $q,t$-Catalan polynomial (https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.00577)\nciteturn2academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.3 years ago; Authors: Graham Hawkes ... The conjecture posits that $\\mathcal{C}_{r/s}$ can be written in terms of symmetric monomial strings indexed by maximal Dyck paths.\nTitle: A conjectured formula for the rational $q,t$-Catalan polynomial\nAuthors: Graham Hawkes\nDate: Mon Aug  1 02:28:35 2022\n\nWe conjecture a formula for the rational $q,t$-Catalan polynomial $\\mathcal{C}_{r/s}$ that is symmetric in $q$ and $t$ by definition. The conjecture posits that $\\mathcal{C}_{r/s}$ can be written in terms of symmetric monomial strings indexed by maximal Dyck paths. We show that for any finite $d^*$, giving a combinatorial proof of our conjecture on the infinite set of functions $\\{ \\mathcal{C}_{r/s}^d: r\\equiv 1 \\mod s, \\,\\,\\, d \\leq d^*\\}$ is equivalent to a finite counting problem.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA conjectured formula for the rational $q,t$-Catalan polynomial | alphaXiv (https://www.alphaxiv.org/abs/2208.00577v2)\nciteturn2search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.7 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Graham Hawkes ... The conjecture posits that $\\mathcal{C}_{r/s}$C r/s​ can be written in terms of symmetric monomial strings indexed by maximal Dyck paths.\nSubmitted 09 Feb 2023\n\n# A conjectured formula for the rational $q,t$q,t-Catalan polynomial\n\nGH\n\nGraham Hawkes\n\n## Abstract\n\nWe conjecture a formula for the rational $q,t$q,t-Catalan polynomial $\\mathcal{C}_{r/s}$C r/s​ that is symmetric in $q$q and $t$t by definition. The conjecture posits that $\\mathcal{C}_{r/s}$C r/s​ can be written in terms of symmetric monomial strings indexed by maximal Dyck paths. We show that for any finite $d^*$d∗, giving a combinatorial proof of our conjecture on the infinite set of functions $\\{ \\mathcal{C}_{r/s}^d: r\\equiv 1 \\mod s, \\,\\,\\, d \\leq